{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"GHSA-h57j-5f5m-789v","published":"2026-11-20T23:46:56Z","modified":"2026-11-21T00:00:04.197001984Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-104884"],"summary":"contao/core-bundle: Cross-site scripting in the frontend search results","details":"Commit `23e8cca3136a` hardened the search-result title against insert-tag/XSS by setting `$objTemplate->title = StringUtil::specialchars(StringUtil::stripInsertTags($arrResult[$i]['title']))`. But the legacy HTML5 template does not use that `title` variable - it prints the raw `link` variable, which is assigned without escaping.\n\n## Impact\n\nAffected configuration (important): on 5.7.9 the default search template is the Twig `search_default.html.twig`, which does not use the raw `link` variable and auto-escapes - so a default Twig install is not affected. The vulnerable raw echo is in the legacy `search_default.html5` template (still shipped and selectable in 5.7.9, line 8: `<?= $this->link ?>`); exploitation requires that legacy template to be active for the search module (common on sites migrated from earlier Contao / using custom template selection). Where the legacy template is used, the sink is unambiguously raw and `ModuleSearch::compile()` assigns `link` from the entity-decoded indexed title.\n\nA backend page editor can store script that executes for anonymous front-end visitors (and admins) viewing search results, a stored XSS crossing the editor -> anonymous-visitor boundary.\n\n## Credits\n\nThis security vulnerability was found by @HDWSec","affected":[{"package":{"name":"contao/core-bundle","ecosystem":"Packagist","purl":"pkg:composer/contao/core-bundle"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"4.9.0"},{"fixed":"5.3.50"}]}],"versions":["4.10.0","4.10.0-RC1","4.10.0-RC2","4.10.0-RC3","4.10.0-RC4","4.10.1","4.10.2","4.10.3","4.10.4","4.10.5","4.10.6","4.10.7","4.11.0","4.11.0-RC1","4.11.0-RC2","4.11.1","4.11.2","4.11.3","4.11.4","4.11.5","4.11.6","4.11.7","4.11.8","4.11.9","4.12.0","4.1